  },
  {
    "description": "Decide something waiting on the user, by the ref a list or get result gave: approve or reject (accept and discard for a draft or a runbook proposal, resolve or reject for a decision, with what was decided and why as the note), or deliver an approved change. The user confirms on a card that shows what it is (with its amount where it has one) and may flip the decision or add a note there. List what is waiting first. Here it decides: hitl-approval, a pending transaction (approve or reject; the card shows its amount); change, an agent change (approve, reject, or deliver once approved); runbook-proposal, a runbook proposal (accept or reject; a rejection needs a note); proposal, a graph change proposal (approve or reject); consult, an agent's question (approve, the user's spoken answer as the note); design, a design thread (approve or reject the sign-off); decision, a waiting decision (resolve with an option, or the outcome and why as note; or reject).",
    "name": "decide",
    "parameters": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "decision": {
          "description": "What the user decided (resolve is a decision's approve).",
          "enum": [
            "approve",
            "reject",
            "accept",
            "discard",
            "deliver",
            "resolve",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "note": {
          "description": "The user's note or reason (a consult's answer, a decision's outcome and why).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
        "option": {
          "description": "A decision option, by number or label.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
        "ref": {
          "description": "The row to decide: a ref or a position in the last result.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "scope": {
          "description": ""this-page": a position in ref counts among the rows the page in view shows.",
          "enum": [
            "this-page",
            null,
          ],
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "ref",
        "decision",
        "note",
        "scope",
        "option",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "strict": true,
    "type": "function",
  },
  {
    "description": "Create a record of one kind through the form its page uses, with the fields that kind takes. The user confirms on a card that shows exactly what will be created (an access request's approvers and conflicts first). The kinds here and their fields: work-item (title, initiative?, type?); comment (on, text); saved-search (name, query); sprint (initiative, name, startsOn, endsOn); meeting (initiative, time, thread?); access-request (item, justification, duration?); document (initiative?, title?); whiteboard (initiative?, title?); deck (initiative?, focus?).",
